From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: CE RX fragment caches in every mode, drained under ce_lock

kuncy7's 999-997 gives each CE pipe its own RX page-frag cache, but only
while the NSS 256 MiB profile is active (ab->nss.enabled). Host-mode Wi-Fi
(nss_offload=0, forced with a station interface) keeps dev_alloc_skb() and
the shared per-CPU chunks that ring buffers pin for minutes. Use the private
cache in every mode, as rd03v2's former 984 did.

999-997 drains the cache without ce_lock. The RX replenish timer is not
stopped by ath11k_pcic_stop() (QCN6122) nor by
ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(), and it refills through
ath11k_ce_rx_post_pipe(), which allocates from the same cache under
ce_lock. page_frag_cache has no locking of its own, so take ce_lock around
the drain too.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.c
@@ -329,9 +329,6 @@
 	unsigned int len;
 	void *data;
 
-	if (!ath11k_nss_256m_enabled(pipe->ab))
-		return dev_alloc_skb(pipe->buf_sz);
-
 	lockdep_assert_held(&pipe->ab->ce.ce_lock);
 
 	len = SKB_HEAD_ALIGN(pipe->buf_sz + NET_SKB_PAD);
@@ -904,8 +901,13 @@
 		dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 	}
 
-	/* Also when NSS was turned off for recovery: no-op if unused */
+	/* page_frag_alloc() on this cache runs under ce_lock, and the RX
+	 * replenish timer can still refill the pipe here: ath11k_pcic_stop()
+	 * and the crash path do not stop it. Drain under the same lock.
+	 */
+	spin_lock_bh(&ab->ce.ce_lock);
 	page_frag_cache_drain(&pipe->rx_frag_cache);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->ce.ce_lock);
 }
 
 static void ath11k_ce_shadow_config(struct ath11k_base *ab)
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ce.h
@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@
 	struct ath11k_ce_ring *dest_ring;
 	struct ath11k_ce_ring *status_ring;
 	u64 timestamp;
-	/* NSS 256 MiB profile: RX buffers of this pipe only, under ce_lock */
+	/* RX buffers of this pipe only, in every mode; under ce_lock */
 	struct page_frag_cache rx_frag_cache;
 };
 
